WEBVTT

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.720
It's been over a year since the war with the Jovian lizards began.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.530
The United Forces were so unreliable,

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:16.210
That a civilian corporation Nergal Heavy Industries, built and launched a new battleship.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.900
That's the story so far.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:18.950
But...

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.180
A civilian battleship in times like these?

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.850
What was Nergal thinking?!

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:03.260
With that power we can't leave Nadesico alone!

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.690
As I understand it, the captain of that ship is your daughter.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.610
If the captain of the Nadesico

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.320
requests to be incorporated in the United Forces, then we'll accept.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.350
Admiral...

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.030
We launch at once.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:20.580
Capture the battleship Nadesico.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:22.710
Leave the "Blue Earth" to Me

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.800
Not that I really care, but who named this ship "Nadesico?"

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.020
Leave the "Blue Earth" to Me

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.460
Yeah, that's it. Take your time with it.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.560
Damn it! What are you doing?!

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.170
So, what will happen to me?

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:38.180
To begin with, you piloted the robot,

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.940
and you've done a lot of things that we're not happy about.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:41.680
But we're not soldiers, so...

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.050
SHUT UP!

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.930
Why are there no punishments?

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.080
He stole my starring moment!

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.900
Who's the one who broke his own leg?

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.210
And anyway, this kid is cocky!

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.780
Call captain by her first name.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.680
We need you to stand by as a backup pilot at least until we get more pilots.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.000
You'll be paid more than if you worked as a cook.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.290
But I am a cook.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.700
I just want to become a cook.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.370
We have the Nadesico on our scopes.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.540
Unable to determine its destination.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.320
Take care that we are not detected by their radar.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.650
Chulip ahead. No signs of life.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:19.880
After the Tobiume emerges from the ocean,

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.810
the remaining frigates shall stand by just below the water's surface.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.240
It's been awhile, Yurika.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.560
I wonder how you are doing now.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:36.820
Akito? Akito?

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.330
Really! Akito is holding himself back from seeing me just because I'm the captain.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.110
Hi..!

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:49.120
I know, damn it.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.600
Give me a minute!

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.410
Oh, that's right. I'm the captain, so I have a master key!

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:02.760
You...

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.280
BAKA-bakka!

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.390
Well, you are a healthy man after all.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.280
I'll let it slide this time.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:15.420
What's that supposed to mean?

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.680
Yurika, this is all because...

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.460
I'm so happy! You're calling me "Yurika!"

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:24.860
On Mars, you used to follow me calling "Yurika! Yurika!"

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.570
Akito! Akito!

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.430
Come on, wait for me, Akito!

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.720
Akito, you jerk!

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.020
Wasn't it like this?

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.220
Is that so?

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:40.480
Oh well, no matter.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.680
I'm just so glad I found you.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.380
I tried to contact you many times.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:51.470
Then, my father told me that the Tenkawa household was wiped out on Mars.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:54.110
But you are fine.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.670
When did you come to Earth?

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.920
How can you say this!

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.890
What is it? Why are you angry?

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:06.070
Please listen to me! Akito!

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.240
Hey, Akito. Hey, Akito!

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:11.560
Hey, Akito!

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:12.790
I said listen to me!

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.210
What's wrong with you?!

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.430
You keep ignoring me.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.840
Please tell me. What happened?

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.340
What are you so angry about? Tell me!

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.750
All right, I'll tell you.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:26.760
But first!

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:28.590
Empty cans...

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:29.570
Go in the recycling bin!

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.570
My father and mother were murdered.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.770
They died when your family left Mars.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:44.250
That day, when we saw you off at the airport...

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.690
I want to know the truth. The one who killed my parents...

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:33.400
Depend on what I learn, I might have to kill you.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:34.820
Kill me?

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:36.810
You mean...

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.720
I'll kill you.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:40.920
Darling!

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:45.910
Oh my! It sounds so hard-boiled and romantic!

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.450
I'm Tenkawa Akito.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.410
I humbly submit my services!

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:53.680
Hey, hey...

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.390
Captain, please report to the bridge.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:59.530
Supposedly there is a very important announcement to be made.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:00.130
Announcement?

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:03.400
The reason why we've kept the Nadesico's destination a secret

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.070
was to foil people who want to thwart our mission.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:10.990
Nergal did not build this battleship to participate in Earth's current actions.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:16.410
We will be part of Schiaparelli Project operating independent of the military.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.830
Schiaparelli?

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.850
Our destination is Mars.

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.250
Hey, you! Get back to work!

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.420
I can go back to Mars!

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:30.510
Are we just going to ignore the invasion that threatens the Earth?

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:34.100
Even now, there are countless settlers on both the Moon and Mars.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.940
The UEAF have abandoned them in favor of the defense of Earth.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:41.270
What has become of the resources and the people left on Mars?

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.840
My guess is that they're dead.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:45.980
I don't know. But I believe that it is worthwhile to...

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.440
You'll do no such thing!

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:53.940
Munetake! Have you gone mad?!

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.580
Admiral, we'll be taking control of this ship now.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:07:59.870
What can you do with so few men?

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:03.150
I got it! You must be Jovian spies!

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.490
Don't take this wrong.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:05.900
See?

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:06.590
Here she comes.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:17.520
Note: UESF = United Earth Space Forces
This is Admiral Misumaru, Commander, Third Fleet, UESF.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:19.000
Father!

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:22.100
Father, what's this all about?

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.280
Oh, Yurika, are you doing well?

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:24.980
Yes!

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.120
This is my duty. Please forgive me.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.530
Papa is not happy about this either.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.940
This is very distressing. We thought we had an agreement with the UEAF.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:36.120
Nergal was to use the Nadesico for private projects.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:40.920
Right now, we need weapons that are effective against the Jovian Lizards.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.590
How can we let civilians control a ship such as that?

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:45.480
As expect from Admiral, so straight.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.800
This calls for negotiations, let's discuss at your ship!

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.710
Very well, but the control key and the captain be in our custody!

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:54.390
Let's see now.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.240
Captain, are you going to do as they say?!

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:59.720
Yurika, what Admiral Misumaru says makes sense!

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:01.810
What's the point of having a ship like this head to Mars?

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:06.320
We do not belong to the military.
We have no reason to follow their orders.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.190
Fukube-san, why must you continue to bring shame on your name?

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:11.240
Yurika!

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:14.860
I've never said something wrong, right?

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:21.190
Stop it, Captain!

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.570
Don't do it, Captain!

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:24.430
Captain, this is a trap!

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:25.790
Don't pull it out!

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:30.540
I've pulled it out!

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:33.350
M.. my justice...

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:36.030
Uh oh, there goes the engine.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:39.850
This leaves the Nadesico completely vulnerable.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:45.740
You understand now. Behave yourself inside here.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.420
Damn it! I'll make sure you regret this!

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:52.630
So, the dream for freedom ends in one day, huh?

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:53.930
Don't give up already!

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:56.110
There's always hope!

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:56.870
Sure, sure.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.720
Everyone, don't lose hope yet!

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:00.360
I'm so disappointed.
Evils never win!................. Give me some milk, milk...

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.520
I expected to meet some cool men on a battleship.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:03.920
Well, life's like that.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:06.090
Evils never win!................. Give me some milk, milk...

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:08.040
This ship sure is full of strange characters.

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:12.080
I'm worried about that Nergal guy with the beard and glasses.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:13.720
He sure doesn't look very reliable.

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:16.650
You shouldn't judge a book by its cover, Megu-chan.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:18.890
You never know. It'll be okay!

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.800
What are you doing, being depressed like that?!

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:27.020
All right, I'll show you my special video! It's sure to cheer you up!

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:32.220
Tenkawa, looks like something is starting.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.680
Some kind of video, he said.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:42.870
This is such an old video format, it's going to be tough to get this to work with a modern TV.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.190
All right, it's ready!

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:45.290
Okay!

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:47.210
Watch and be amazed!

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:50.870
Disk, insert! Switch on!

00:11:14.470 --> 00:11:15.540
What is this?

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.360
The neglected classic, Gekiganger 3!

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:21.740
This thirty-nine episode series is a real heart grabber!

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.690
The opening looks different.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:26.100
You can tell?

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:29.260
The real opening comes after episode 3.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.840
Oh, it's you.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:36.300
You have no right to talk about Gekiganger!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.910
You forgot your crutch.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.030
I do too! I saw the series as a boy growing up on Mars.

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:43.590
Then why aren't you into being a robot pilot?

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.000
Who cares about being a cook?!

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:46.470
What's wrong with being a cook?!

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.300
Invincible! Gekiganger takes off!

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:54.730
Baka!

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:56.640
UESF Third Fleet Flagship Tobiume

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:57.540
Tobiume's Conspiring Room

00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:59.460
I wonder what's keeping Jun and the others?

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:01.300
Now just calm yourself.

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:03.750
I must say, Yurika, it looks as if you've lost weight.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:06.200
It's been only two days since I left you, Father.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:10.620
Well anyway, you must be very hungry. Go ahead and let yourself go!

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:14.540
There's strawberry shortcake, chocolate cake and cheesecake!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.480
There is lots and lots for you to enjoy!

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:20.080
Say, Father, do you recall Tenkawa Akito-kun?

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:21.040
Tenkawa?

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.990
Tenkawa, who's he?

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:25.960
He was the son of the family next door to us on Mars.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:26.470
Mars?

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:28.390
I've just met Akito.

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:34.430
You really are something, Gekiganger.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:35.820
Now, finish me off!

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:38.860
Stop! Don't kill Rokudo-niisan!

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.470
Ken, please stop!

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:42.660
Ken!

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:46.040
Man, just take a look at the suspense that builds here!

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.470
It's pretty predictable, but still...

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.850
Shut up! Be honest and just enjoy it!

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:50.570
Sure, sure.

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:52.450
Nana!

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:54.250
Be honest and enjoy.

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:56.670
Gekiganger, you jerk!

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:58.340
Murdered?

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:02.050
Yes, do you know anything, Father?

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.390
There must be some mistake.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:05.480
It was very clear that the Tenkawas died in an accident.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.250
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.360
Have you arrived at a conclusion?

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.990
Yes. We discussed the issue at length.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:12.660
And?

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:18.440
Nadesico is private property, and no restrictions should be placed on it.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:22.070
Gekigan Punch!

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:24.320
Gekigan Cutters!

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.730
Gekigan Beam!

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:28.400
The natural Earth!

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:29.910
The blue Earth!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.160
We will protect it!

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:34.110
These guys are so passionate.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:37.260
Do they yell out the attacks because they're using voice commands?

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:38.580
No, no!

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.970
This is what guts and courage are all about!

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:43.000
What the soul pours forth!

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:48.300
C'mon, everyone! Doesn't this intense situation get to you?!

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:50.170
A secret base stolen!

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:51.470
A military conspiracy!

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:56.760
Do you think the remaining children would try to resolve the situation?

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:58.410
What children?

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:01.830
But you know, this ship won't budge unless the Captain comes back.

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:03.240
You can do everything with guts!

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.220
What's wrong, everyone?

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:08.090
This is a situation that screams out drama and excitement!

00:14:13.350 --> 00:14:17.030
I'll take off in the robot, and bring the Captain back.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:20.290
I want to help Mars.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.300
Even if the rest of the world is only thinking about the war.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:26.660
There must be something else you can do.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:32.100
Everyone, isn't that what all of you came here for?

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.230
A Chulip?

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:42.230
Ship out of control! Repeating...

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:45.150
Frigates Crocus and Pansy have been caught!
Ship out of control! Repeating...

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:47.560
Those bastards are here.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.200
Pansy and Crocus have disappeared!
Ready the Nadesico for launch!

00:14:58.200 --> 00:14:59.990
All right, Yurika, give me the key now.

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:01.560
What?

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:02.540
Where is Yurika?

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.440
I'm here, Father.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.320
Yurika!

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:07.590
I will ask you once more.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.970
It's concerning Akito's parents.

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:12.920
Yurika, is this the right time for that?

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.300
This is something very important to me.

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:16.680
The Chulip is heading toward the Nadesico.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.810
Father, tell me the truth!

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.060
Yurika...

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:27.540
I may have heard such a story before,
but I didn't want to break your heart, and so...

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:28.810
I understand.

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:29.500
Let's go!

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:29.980
Aye, aye!

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:33.580
Everyone, get back! Get back!

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.570
Wait! Where do you think you're going?

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:37.710
The Nadesico.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:38.490
What?!..

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:41.240
Yurika, aren't you going to surrender the ship to the Admiral?

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:45.710
I only came to find out more about Akito's story.

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:47.170
Yurika!

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:52.470
A captain does not abandon her ship under any circumstances!

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.050
You were the one that taught me that!

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:58.270
Besides, someone special to me is on that ship.

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.190
Wha...!

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.150
Thank you. I'm good to go.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:04.270
Follow the instructions of the crew!

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:05.320
Launching Aestivalis.

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:08.030
We have no idea what will happen next,
so please evacuate!

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:11.600
Hey, Ruri-chan, are you smiling?

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:12.280
Not really.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.160
I guess I'm quite a fool myself.

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:20.000
V!

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:23.960
I'm coming back now. Please ready the deck!

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:26.060
They've taken over the hangar.

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:26.800
An Aestivalis...

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:28.380
Just give yourself up.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:31.060
Houmei-san!

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:33.610
That was easy!

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:34.400
V!

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:35.760
Here I go!

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:37.680
On your mark.

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:40.540
Prepare manual launch.

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:41.350
Go!

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:44.720
So manual launching just means he goes running out of here.

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:45.290
Yeah.

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.020
Wait a minute!

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:49.440
Tenkawa, that one's in land equipment!

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.150
It hasn't been reconfigured!

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:56.700
One, two...

00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:58.320
Go!

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.200
Fly!

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.170
I told you, that thing's in its land fighting configuration!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.490
Land engagement mode!

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:11.560
What? What's going on?!

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:16.890
Come on! Fly! I said fly!

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:29.530
Akito, are you going to be a decoy again?

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:30.840
What?

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:33.720
I'll use this opportunity to board the Nadesico!

00:17:35.300 --> 00:17:36.570
What the hey?

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.580
Hey, just a second!

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.640
Like I said, it's in land engagement mode!

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.170
Akito, you're putting your life on the line for me again!

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:51.840
What is that?

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:54.220
Oh...

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:57.140
He sure has a lot of energy jumping around like that.

00:17:57.140 --> 00:17:59.060
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:00.230
Yahoo!

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:06.310
Electrical charge normal. Re-starting Phase Transition engine.

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:07.600
System coming back on line.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.250
All just perfect!

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:13.100
We're moving right along! Full speed ahead!

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:16.900
Before we do, Yamada Jirou-san is asking permission to take off.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:17.490
Yamada?

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.950
My name is Daigoji Gai!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:22.110
I'm all set to go. Let's do it!

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:25.600
Don't give up!

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:28.410
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:30.590
Gekigan Wing!

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:33.810
All right.

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:37.220
We're going to dock your cockpit unit with this air combat frame in mid-air.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:38.820
The call will be "Cross Crash!"

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.120
Do I really have to say that?

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:41.060
That's right.

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:42.520
We only get one shot.

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:43.470
My leg won't last long.

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:45.020
Yamada Jirou...

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.150
Gai! Daigoji!

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:49.770
All right! Go!

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:53.610
Fifteen seconds to docking!

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:54.710
Let's go!

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:55.750
Cr... Cr...
Cross Crash!

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:57.790
Louder!

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.530
CROSS CRASH!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.340
Go, Akito!

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:20.930
Gekigan Flare!

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:23.440
GEKIGAN FLARE!

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.340
Go! Go!

00:19:29.090 --> 00:19:30.550
No way!

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:33.680
A high speed attack using the distortion field.

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.640
What's a Gekigan Flare?

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:37.810
WE can't be left behind, full speed ahead!

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:38.820
You're serious?

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:39.740
Go!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.490
Hey, stop!

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:46.090
What are you doing?! . . .  Hey, wait! Stop I tell you!

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:47.800
Gravity Blast, stand by.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.550
Roger. Gravity Blast charging.

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:50.560
What are you doing?! . . .  Hey, wait! Stop I tell you!

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:54.540
Yurika!

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:08.640
A Gravity Blast from inside?

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.560
What is she thinking?

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:13.530
Too cool.

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:16.420
Recover Akito's Aestivalis.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:18.990
Ano, Daigoji-san took off as well.

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:20.600
Get him along the way.

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:22.530
Yamada-san, Nice work.

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:24.170
Daigoji Gai!

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.070
Admiral, should we pursue her?

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:29.120
Pursue?

00:20:29.470 --> 00:20:31.500
What's the point when we haven't got a chance against her?

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.940
This operation was a failure.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.320
So, who is this person she's crazy about?

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.570
Aoi-kun, would you happen to know?

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:38.960
Yurika...

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:49.600
Tears. Oh, the tears that are shed!

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:54.580
Have you seen the tears shed by lovers separated by battle lines?

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:56.430
The passionate cry of the young officer!

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:59.150
The anticipation of forbidden love by the maiden!

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:03.450
Witness the outcome of the stratospheric romance of the century!

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:06.380
Have three handkerchiefs ready for the climax of the next episode!

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:08.690
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:10.580
"A Goodbye that Came Too Soon!"

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.960
Let's watch it, everyone!
